  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0228_e44d16033183.png\" style=\"width: 328px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>The compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;steam volatile. It is due to the presence of intramolecular hydrogen bonding in the compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>. Hence, the above mixture can be separated by steam distillation.</p>"
